rthwest entrance and choose among the library’s quiet, limited-talking, or group-study areas.","short_summary":"A science-focused ground-floor library with distinct zones for silent, conversational, and collaborative work.","evidence_claim":"IU Libraries locates the Sciences Library in the Chemistry Building, while its current quiet policy identifies quiet, limited-talking, and group-study areas within the library.","source_url":"https://libraries.indiana.edu/sciences-library","source_title":"Sciences Library","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Located in room C002 at the northwest corner of the Chemistry Building’s ground floor; follow interior signage after entering from the ramped northwest entrance.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"iu-wells-east-tower-quiet-floors","subject_type":"study_space","entity_name":"Wells Library East Tower Quiet Floors","title":"Match Your Reading to the Stacks","subtitle":"Herman B Wells Library, East Tower floors 4–10","notes":"Pick a quiet upper floor near the research collection you need, then settle into one of the tower’s individual study spaces.","short_summary":"Seven quiet stack floors combine individual work areas with subject-arranged research collections.","evidence_claim":"IU Libraries designates East Tower floors 4 through 10 as quiet-study space and identifies the upper East Tower as home to research stacks and numerous quiet study areas.","source_url":"https://libraries.indiana.edu/herman-b-wells-library","source_title":"Herman B Wells Library","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use the Wells Library East Tower elevators for floors 4–10. These floors are designated quiet study areas; group work belongs in designated West Tower zones.","co